    "stem": "Uma knows a straight angle at point $O$ is $180^\\circ$. Ray $OP$ cuts it into adjacent angles $\\angle AOP$ and $\\angle POB$, and $\\angle AOP=70^\\circ$.\n\nWhich claim finds $\\angle POB$?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Call the answer the \"whole angle\" $180^\\circ$, without subtracting the known adjacent part.",
      "B": "Say that finding $\\angle POB$ is what creates the straight $180^\\circ$ angle at $O$, instead of using the whole to find the unknown part.",
      "C": "The adjacent parts add to the whole: $\\angle POB=180^\\circ-70^\\circ=110^\\circ$.",
      "D": "Report $70^\\circ$ as $\\angle POB$ only because $70$ is the printed degree number in the stem."
    },
